  eprint    = {2205.10625},
  note      = {Google Research / UC Berkeley / UNC; introduces the two-stage sequential-decomposition prompt: (1) emit ordered subproblem list, (2) solve each subproblem conditioned on all prior subproblem answers (chained-answer propagation); on GPT-3 code-davinci-002 it lifts SCAN compositional-split accuracy from ~16\% (standard prompting) to ~99.7\% and GSM8K from ~49.5\% (CoT) to ~62.4\%; strict generalization of P-90 CoT in the single-subproblem degenerate case; distinct from P-62 Decomposed Prompting (independent modular prompts) in that answers are prefix-conditioned, not sampled independently; the SLM-era chained-decomposition anchor for MAgHARCM's PRIM-1 reverse-topological planner and PRIM-23 chunked translation.}
}
